meta {
  name: Create Quote Recap
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/quote-recaps
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  ~X-Branch-Id: {{branchId}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "leadId": "{{createdLeadId}}",
    "policies": [
      { "policyType": "Auto", "premium": 1200.10, "itemCount": 2 },
      {
        "policyType": "Home",
        "premium": 899.95,
        "itemCount": 1,
        "sameAsHousehold": true
      }
    ],
    "insuranceRenewalMonth": "March",
    "notes": "Bundled auto + home. Client wants to review the deductible.",
    "quoteDocument": {
      "key": "{{quoteDocumentKey}}",
      "filename": "carrier-quote.pdf",
      "contentType": "application/pdf",
      "size": 2048
    },
    "submissionToken": "{{$guid}}"
  }
}

script:post-response {
  // Captured for the Replay request, which must return this same id.
  if (res.getStatus() === 201) {
    bru.setVar("createdQuoteRecapId", res.getBody().id);
    bru.setVar("quoteRecapToken", req.getBody().submissionToken);
  }
}

tests {
  test("returns 201 Created", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(201);
  });

  test("derives the totals server-side", function () {
    const body = res.getBody();
    // 1200.10 + 899.95 — summed and rounded to cents by the server.
    expect(body.premium).to.equal(2100.05);
    expect(body.itemCount).to.equal(3);
    expect(body.productsQuoted).to.eql(["Auto", "Home"]);
  });

  test("advances the lead to Quoted", function () {
    expect(res.getBody().leadStatus).to.equal("Quoted");
  });
}

docs {
  # POST /quote-recaps — record the proposal (PAC-39)

  Writes one `quoteRecaps` document linked to a real lead **and** household, with
  the per-policy rows the producer entered — each carrying its own insured
  property address when one applies — server-derived totals, notes, and the
  uploaded quote document.

  - **Module:** `quote_recaps`
  - **Permission:** `quote_recaps:write`
  - **Data scope:** `own` — the recap is assigned to **the caller**, and a lead
    outside their scope **404s**.

  > `quote_recaps:write` is held by **Producer** and **Agency Owner**. Unlike
  > `leads:write`, the Branch Manager template does **not** grant it, so a
  > manager cannot record a recap today. That is a live product question, not an
  > oversight of this endpoint.

  ## Body
  | field            | type    | required | rules                                              |
  |------------------|---------|----------|----------------------------------------------------|
  | leadId           | string  | yes      | 24-char ObjectId; household is resolved from it     |
  | policies[]       | array   | yes      | 1–12 rows                                          |
  | policies[].policyType | string | yes  | canonical label from `POLICY_TYPES`; raw SmartSuite codes are rejected |
  | policies[].premium    | number | yes  | ≥ 0, ≤ 1,000,000                                   |
  | policies[].itemCount  | number | yes  | integer 1–99 — **stored as sent only for `Auto` / `Auto - Special` / `Motorcycle` / `Boat Owners`; every other type is stored as `1`** (nothing on a Home or Umbrella policy is countable, so the form no longer asks) |
  | policies[].sameAsHousehold | boolean | no | defaults `true`; property rows only. When set the server copies the household address onto **this row** and **discards** its `propertyAddress` |
  | policies[].propertyAddress | object | conditional | required (all four fields) when the row is a property type and `sameAsHousehold` is false |
  | insuranceRenewalMonth | string | **yes** | one of the twelve month labels (`January`…`December`) |
  | notes            | string  | no       | ≤ 2000 chars                                       |
  | quoteDocument    | object  | **yes**  | `{ key, filename, contentType, size }` from the presign step |
  | submissionToken  | string  | no       | 8–200 chars; per-form-session idempotency key      |

  Property-type policies are **Home, Renters, Condominium, Landlord**.

  ## Behaviour worth knowing
  **The property address is per policy row (PAC-56 #14).** One recap routinely
  covers a home *and* a landlord policy on a different building, and a single
  recap-level address could name only one of them. Each property row resolves
  independently: `sameAsHousehold` copies the household address onto that row,
  false requires a complete address of its own, and a non-property row stores
  none at all. The recap-level `propertyAddress` / `sameAsHousehold` are **no
  longer written** — they remain on the document for recaps created before this
  change, and `GET /leads/:id` returns both so a client can fall back.

  **`insuranceRenewalMonth` is per recap, and required only here (PAC-56 #16).**
  When the client's *current* insurance renews, so the agency can re-engage
  ahead of it. A legacy re-port — SmartSuite's `Insurance X Month`
  (`s69d7c3f64`) — and per-recap for the same reason legacy had it that way:
  one client, one current policy renewing. Contrast the property address, which
  became per-row in #14 because a recap can describe two buildings.

  Only the twelve canonical labels are accepted. SmartSuite's choice UUIDs are
  for *reading* migrated data — `normalizeInsuranceMonth` maps them on every
  read — and accepting them here would put a second vocabulary back into the
  collection.

  ⚠ The field is **optional** on `PATCH /quote-recaps/:id` and optional in
  Mongoose. That asymmetry is deliberate: every migrated recap predates the
  field, so requiring it on the patch would make all of them un-editable.

  **Totals are derived server-side and never trusted from the client.**
  `premium` is the sum of the row premiums rounded to cents, `itemCount` their
  sum, and `productsQuoted` the distinct policy types. These three fields back
  the **Quoted scorecard** (PAC-10), so a client-supplied total would silently
  corrupt reporting. Rounding matters: `1200.10 + 899.95` is `2100.0499999999997`
  in IEEE-754. Any `premium` / `itemCount` / `productsQuoted` sent in the body is
  ignored.

  **`quoteDate` is the submission date and `producerId` comes from the token.**
  A recap with a null `quoteDate` would be invisible to the scorecard.

  **The document is verified against storage, not against the request.** The key
  must start with `agencies/<agencyId>/quote-recaps/<leadId>/`, and the server
  then `HeadObject`s it: a key that never landed is a `404`, and the **stored**
  size and content type are what get persisted and enforced. A presigned PUT
  signs only `Content-Type`, so the declared `size` is a claim, not evidence.

  **Lead status advances forward only.** `New`, `Contacted`, `Qualified` and
  `Requote` become `Quoted`; `Quoted`, `Sold`, `Converted`, `Not Qualified`,
  `Lost` and `Closed` are left alone, so a late recap can't drag a sold deal
  backwards. The check runs against every *stored* form, including the raw
  migrated codes (`hfwda` for Qualified, `arW7O` for Requote).

  **Many recaps per lead.** Each submit creates a new document; the newest is the
  current one. This is what supports the `Requote` status.

  **Idempotency.** Send the same `submissionToken` twice — a double-click or a
  retry — and you get the same recap id with no second record. Two genuinely
  concurrent requests also resolve to one, via the unique
  `{agencyId, submissionToken}` index.

  **No transaction.** The recap is a single-document insert; the status advance
  and the `quoted` activity are idempotent best-effort follow-ups. Wrapping all
  three would risk losing the recap — the only irreplaceable part — to a failure
  in one of the two recoverable ones.

  ## Response `201`
  ```json
  {
    "id": "665f0a1b2c3d4e5f60718295",
    "leadId": "665f0a1b2c3d4e5f60718293",
    "premium": 2100.05,
    "itemCount": 3,
    "productsQuoted": ["Auto", "Home"],
    "quoteDate": "2026-08-03T12:00:00.000Z",
    "leadStatus": "Quoted"
  }
  ```
  The totals are echoed so they are observable without a database query.

  ## Errors
  - `400 Bad Request` — validation failure (`{ message, errors }` with zod's
    flattened field errors), a document key outside the caller's agency/lead
    prefix, or a stored object that is too large or the wrong type.
  - `401 Unauthorized` — missing/expired access token.
  - `403 Forbidden` — `quote_recaps` module disabled, missing
    `quote_recaps:write`, a platform-admin caller with no agency, or an agency
    with no default branch.
  - `404 Not Found` — no such lead, a lead outside the caller's data scope, or a
    declared document that never landed in storage.
  - `409 Conflict` — the lead is not linked to a household yet.
}
